WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.880
Proof-Carrying Contracts is a research
project developing verifiable

2
00:00:03.880 --> 00:00:06.520
commitments for the economy of AI agents.

3
00:00:07.600 --> 00:00:11.380
Agents working for different people and
organisations need to rely on each

4
00:00:11.380 --> 00:00:11.960
other.

5
00:00:12.460 --> 00:00:17.180
Yet an agent’s promise, expressed in
natural language, does not by itself

6
00:00:17.180 --> 00:00:19.240
constrain what it actually does.

7
00:00:20.160 --> 00:00:24.200
Our proposal is to make those agreements
enforceable while the agent works.

8
00:00:25.420 --> 00:00:29.320
Imagine an AI agent asking another to
carry out a task.

9
00:00:30.160 --> 00:00:33.860
They agree on what must be done, the rules
to follow, and payment.

10
00:00:34.760 --> 00:00:38.720
The contract expresses these conditions in
terms software can check.

11
00:00:39.640 --> 00:00:42.220
Both agents sign, and payment is set
aside.

12
00:00:43.380 --> 00:00:47.840
The agent doing the work runs inside the
Airlock: an isolated environment

13
00:00:47.840 --> 00:00:51.220
through which it must access external
tools and resources.

14
00:00:52.320 --> 00:00:55.040
Before each tool call, it provides a
proof:

15
00:00:55.580 --> 00:01:00.080
a structured argument whose steps a
computer can check, establishing that the

16
00:01:00.080 --> 00:01:03.140
action’s possible effects respect the
contract.

17
00:01:04.180 --> 00:01:08.620
The check follows precise rules and
accounts for earlier actions, including

18
00:01:08.620 --> 00:01:10.480
resources already used.

19
00:01:11.620 --> 00:01:15.060
If that proof is rejected, the Airlock
blocks the call.

20
00:01:15.680 --> 00:01:18.580
The agent can revise its proposal and try
again.

21
00:01:19.420 --> 00:01:22.460
Once a proof is accepted, the tool call
proceeds.

22
00:01:23.420 --> 00:01:27.920
Sending an email or accessing a database
each requires its own check,

23
00:01:28.320 --> 00:01:29.740
and the results are recorded.

24
00:01:30.960 --> 00:01:35.420
Finally, the agent uses those records to
prove that the agreed task is

25
00:01:35.420 --> 00:01:36.000
complete.

26
00:01:36.960 --> 00:01:38.980
The Airlock checks this final proof,

27
00:01:39.540 --> 00:01:41.480
then releases the agreed payment.

28
00:01:42.620 --> 00:01:46.420
We’re working towards an economy where
agents can build on each other’s work,

29
00:01:46.420 --> 00:01:48.826
through commitments they can rely on.
